1
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:50,967
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,386
CANDIDATE 2, PARK HAE-KANG

3
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:56,764
Cheers.

4
00:00:56,765 --> 00:01:00,517
Wait, Mr. Park. This calls for a toast.

5
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,269
A toast? We don't do stuff like that.

6
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,773
Then can I say something instead?

7
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:09,235
Fine.

8
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:11,196
That's great.

9
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:17,534
Everyone, you've all seen headlines like,

10
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:20,163
"Apartment complexes,
a hotbed of corruption!"

11
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:24,958
Not writing up contracts properly,

12
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:28,378
handing no-bid contracts
to favored companies,

13
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:32,257
inflating construction costs,
embezzling maintenance funds…

14
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,843
I don't want to see you guys on the news.

15
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:38,722
So please,
don't get involved in such corruption.

16
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:40,682
- I hope you finish your term
- This is boring.

17
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:42,684
without any trouble, Mr. Park.

18
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:44,686
All right, then. Cheers!

19
00:01:44,687 --> 00:01:46,481
Cheers!

20
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:49,734
Why the long faces?

21
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:54,196
You made an intermittent family
and got the position you wanted so badly.

22
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:55,572
Since it's come to this,

23
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:59,368
I just wanted to encourage you,
as your fake wife, to do your best.

24
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,869
Come on. Cheers!

25
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,998
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

26
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:11,421
How refreshing.

27
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:13,173
Out of everything I've ever done,

28
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:15,092
that was by far the hardest.

29
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:18,054
The packages were piling up
like a mountain…

30
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:21,265
What's with you? Why are you so drunk?

31
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:22,599
He had a tough time.

32
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,519
You have a chili flake
stuck in your teeth.

33
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:26,813
<i>I heard the good news.</i>

34
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:30,692
- Congratulations.
- You already heard?

35
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:35,113
<i>Blood?</i>

36
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:49,669
<i>What's his deal? I'm sure that was blood.</i>

37
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:54,674
I'm almost there.

38
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:57,593
Yong-man…

39
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:58,845
Just focus

40
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,098
on saving Yong-man for now.

41
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:08,229
THE APARTMENT JOB

42
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:18,197
Right. That's nonsense.

43
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:23,244
My elbow's been acting up.
I can't hit the ball well.

44
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,246
- Are you okay?
- Goodness.

45
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,335
Don't feel too upset about this, Mr. Lee.

46
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:34,588
Right now, you're not in a position
to sit at the same table as us.

47
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:36,298
It's just a tiny bump in the road.

48
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:38,634
Mr. Lee wouldn't stumble
over something so small.

49
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:39,719
That'd be embarrassing.

50
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,889
This is so absurd, it's almost comical.

51
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:46,892
In any case, it's no big deal,
so don't worry about it.

52
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:49,687
Eat up. You look so worn out.

53
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:51,397
Yes, sir.

54
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:53,441
Should we have gotten him beef?

55
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:56,569
For workers, pork is still best.

56
00:03:58,154 --> 00:04:02,741
Even with a simple home renovation,
you run into all sorts of issues.

57
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:05,036
But we're developing an entire city.

58
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,703
You know,

59
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:09,457
I just don't like Oman New Town
getting mentioned like this.

60
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:12,793
I don't want this small spark

61
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:16,421
turning into some huge corruption scandal
like in the movies.

62
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:20,802
I want this wrapped up cleanly
without all that nonsense.

63
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:25,139
Wrapping things up cleanly
is my specialty, you know.

64
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:54,294
LEOPARD OF KILIMANJARO

65
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:05,429
<i>Have you ever seen a hyena
Roaming the foothills</i>

66
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:07,681
<i>In search of prey?</i>

67
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:10,935
<i>Hyenas roam the foothills
Only searching for carrion</i>

68
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:14,355
<i>I want to be a leopard, not a hyena</i>

69
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:18,484
- He's inside, right?
- Yes, he is.

70
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:20,819
How is he right now?

71
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,739
<i>I wake up great, then I wake up small</i>

72
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,492
<i>Now, I'm resting
In a dark corner of the world</i>

73
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:33,499
<i>I can't just come like the wind
And leave like morning dew</i>

74
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:38,671
<i>I should leave my mark behind</i>

75
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:43,801
I was feeling a little frustrated,

76
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:47,554
so I wanted to sing this song first.

77
00:05:47,555 --> 00:05:49,557
- Mr. Yoo.
- Yes?

78
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:53,643
Didn't you conduct a cultural heritage
survey before construction started?

79
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:54,811
We did, but--

80
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,938
They found a bowl!

81
00:05:56,939 --> 00:05:59,108
Something that shouldn't have been found!

82
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,910
It's bad enough that I spent my own money
digging up my own land

83
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:12,663
and discovered something
that shouldn't have been there.

84
00:06:14,373 --> 00:06:16,667
- Mr. Choi.
- Yes?

85
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:20,796
How much interest
will I have to pay on my bank loan

86
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,423
while the construction is on hold?

87
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,009
Well…

88
00:06:25,843 --> 00:06:27,929
It's a pretty big amount.

89
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:35,353
It's been a while.
Put your heads in position.

90
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,521
Sir…

91
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,814
Heads in position!

92
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,233
- Yes, sir!
- Move!

93
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:10,054
<i>Love is lonely
Because you bet your fate on it</i>

94
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:14,934
<i>Lonely because you risk everything</i>

95
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:17,395
I'm lonely.

96
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:21,107
I feel like I'm the only one doing my job.

97
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:25,736
Find a way
to resume construction immediately!

98
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:30,240
I'm sorry, sir,
but unless the relics are fake,

99
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:33,911
- there's no way to reverse this!
- Mr. Park!

100
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,998
Please forgive me, sir!

101
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:42,920
Fake?

102
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,216
What? You did what?

103
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:50,343
- A fake wife?
- Yes.

104
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:52,429
It's just like another stand-in gig.

105
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:55,390
I get that you need the money,
but have you lost your mind?

106
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:56,641
You wanted to be a lawyer.

107
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:59,686
I'm going to start studying again
once I get the remaining money.

108
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:01,104
There are only a few days left.

109
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,231
Does Ha-jeong know?

110
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:03,649
Of course not.

111
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:06,443
She's in France right now.

112
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:09,530
I sent her there
with the advance payment I got.

113
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:13,700
Her dream is to be a patissier,
so I told her to go and experience stuff.

114
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:15,160
But why is that guy going so far

115
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:18,455
as to fake a family to become
a residents' association president?

116
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:19,414
What?

117
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:21,082
Just think about it.

118
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:24,337
Why would he pay you that much
just for that position?

119
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:26,714
I know.

120
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:32,052
My mom's acquaintance's
in-law's cousin's friend--

121
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:34,889
Yeong-ju, that's practically a stranger.

122
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:38,475
Right. Anyway, that stranger
became an apartment president

123
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:40,977
and pocketed a huge sum.

124
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:45,649
They even got a new car
and moved to a fancy place too.

125
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,400
- Could he also be--
- Hey.

126
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:49,320
Mr. Park isn't that kind of person.

127
00:08:50,029 --> 00:08:51,447
Why are you shouting at me?

128
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:54,617
Then what kind of man is he, exactly?

129
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:56,827
What?

130
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,830
Well, he's…

131
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:18,099
What is Park Hae-kang doing on my ceiling?

132
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:20,434
Let's just sleep.

133
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:30,777
- I'm here!
- Hi.

134
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:32,654
- I'm not late, am I?
- You are.

135
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:35,031
What? Is it someone's birthday?

136
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:38,326
No, but it's the first day
of our boss's term as president.

137
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:39,828
I put my skills to use

138
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:42,957
to make a hearty meal
to keep our strength up.

139
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,794
Mr. Park, you're drinking
espresso again without eating?

140
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:48,628
I'm fine.

141
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,463
It's not fine with me.

142
00:09:50,464 --> 00:09:52,716
Your brothers prepared
a nice meal for you.

143
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,634
You should at least join them.

144
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:56,012
It's okay.

145
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:58,806
Hey.

146
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:03,686
Come on.

147
00:10:05,187 --> 00:10:07,105
Why are you doing this to me?

148
00:10:07,106 --> 00:10:09,774
It's seaweed soup. It's hot.

149
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:10,610
All right.

150
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:12,736
Here.

151
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,780
Should I feed it to you? Here.

152
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:16,824
I'll eat it myself.

153
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:34,424
This is good.

154
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:36,135
You did great.

155
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:38,679
You finally seem like an ordinary human.

156
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:45,436
Is that shaved ice?

157
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:48,272
I'll give you more.

158
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:50,191
Why are you crying?

159
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,527
This is the first time
you've tried my cooking.

160
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:04,538
So…

161
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,706
Dad.

162
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:07,916
- Yes?
- Yes?

163
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:08,959
Which dad?

164
00:11:09,543 --> 00:11:10,627
- Me?
- Me?

165
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:11,629
What is it?

166
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:15,466
Do you have something to say?

167
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:19,720
Mom.

168
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:25,184
Ms. Kang, Gyeong-buk's calling you.

169
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,188
I'm still not used to being called "Mom."
What is it?

170
00:11:32,983 --> 00:11:34,068
It's nothing.

171
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,198
- I'm getting ready for work.
- Yes, sir.

172
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:41,283
Yes, sir.

173
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:47,455
It looks like
they're from every household.

174
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:51,084
Seems like everyone was desperate
for a change in leadership.

175
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,168
Sang-tae.

176
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:54,337
- Yes?
- Watch your mouth.

177
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:56,881
Someone could hear you. Be careful.

178
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:58,259
But we're the only ones here.

179
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:02,137
- Sorry.
- You should all lie low.

180
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:05,307
A change in leadership
always brings a bloodbath.

181
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,394
I wouldn't go that far…

182
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:16,610
You're all so clueless.

183
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,281
The blood…

184
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,408
What are you waiting for?

185
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:26,245
We should get ready
to welcome the new president.

186
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:27,830
Let's…

187
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:29,707
do a good job.

188
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:37,590
If you don't want that
to happen to you, okay?

189
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:39,925
Here's a gift.

190
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,987
The bloodbath has already begun.

191
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:03,365
Is it cold now?

192
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:06,368
It's nice and cold.

193
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:10,331
- Hold up.
- You scared me.

194
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:14,168
It's okay to drink by yourself,

195
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:18,964
but don't gamble at the senior center.

196
00:13:21,634 --> 00:13:23,219
I won't.

197
00:13:23,802 --> 00:13:26,429
I don't even have the money for that.

198
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:27,388
I can't.

199
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:30,809
You're someone to gamble
even if you're broke.

200
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:34,104
If the boss finds out, you're dead.

201
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:35,689
All right.

202
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:38,441
Dad.

203
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:40,693
Let me talk to your grandpa for a second.

204
00:13:40,694 --> 00:13:42,196
Okay.

205
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:46,199
Ms. Kang, aren't you getting ready?

206
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,535
Getting ready for what?

207
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:49,995
We have to go to the management office.

208
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:54,040
What? Mr. Park's the president.
Why would we go there?

209
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:57,168
It's his first day of work.
We should go and support him.

210
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,463
And something might happen to him,

211
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:02,298
so we should show him
that we have his back.

212
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:05,260
Heading to work on his first day
with the support of his family…

213
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:07,012
- Wouldn't it be a beautiful sight?
- Yeah.

214
00:14:07,805 --> 00:14:09,180
What do you mean by "beautiful"?

215
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:12,433
It would be weird for a grown man's
entire family to follow him to work.

216
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:14,602
But it's nothing hard to do.
You're getting paid.

217
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:16,771
You should at least
do some things that we ask.

218
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:20,733
Employees also have the right
to refuse unreasonable or unfair demands.

219
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:21,693
Unbelievable.

220
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,319
Neglect of duty, dereliction of duty.

221
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,780
That's what you're doing right now,
Ms. Kang Ha-ri.

222
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,740
As you may have noticed,
he went to law school.

223
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,493
- Gosh.
- She should know too.

224
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:33,079
Hey. Dereliction of duty
applies only to public officials.

225
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,415
I'm not working as a public official here.

226
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:36,917
How can you not know that?

227
00:14:37,918 --> 00:14:41,129
As you may have noticed,
she also attended law school.

228
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:42,756
They should know too.

229
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:46,384
Well, you're not an employee,
to be precise.

230
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:48,387
How can you not know that?

231
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:50,848
Oh, right. You failed the bar exam.

232
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,684
What did you just say?

233
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:57,938
I'll support him in my own way,
so just know that.

234
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:21,754
You look nice, Mr. Park.

235
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:24,256
You've succeeded, thanks to me.

236
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,637
Mr. Park!

237
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:34,641
True Value State's residents' association
president, Park Hae-kang!

238
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:36,976
Good luck today!

239
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:39,355
You look so cool, Hae-kang!

240
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:50,783
Ha-ri, bring in the laundry.

241
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:58,540
I can't believe I just did that.

242
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:02,710
But did all of them know
that I failed the bar exam?

243
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:04,004
Darn it!

244
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:09,592
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

245
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:12,387
<i>With the president's seal,
the facility manager's seal,</i>

246
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:16,475
<i>and the apartment complex bank book,
this will all be over.</i>

247
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:18,602
<i>Let's go.</i>

248
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,732
Good morning!

249
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:26,401
Hello.

250
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:27,777
Everyone's here again.

251
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:29,446
Welcome, President Park.

252
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:32,199
Your family's here too.

253
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,785
- You really are…
- Hello!

254
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:36,704
a close-knit family.

255
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:39,956
- Are you busy, Mr. Choi?
- Not at all.

256
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:42,376
I was just stamping
some payroll paperwork.

257
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,922
Come on, Sang-tae.
Give him the thing we prepared.

258
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:50,383
- Congratulations, President Park.
- Thank you.

259
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:52,970
- It looks great on you.
- Thank you.

260
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:03,396
I hope you like your office.

261
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:05,274
I love it, Mr. Choi.

262
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:10,945
And here.

263
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:13,531
There are some basic handover notes,

264
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:17,326
along with the bank book
and your stamp too.

265
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:19,913
I look forward to working with you, sir.

266
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:34,887
The power of the president.

267
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:36,513
Pardon?

268
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:43,604
You're always so interesting.

269
00:17:44,605 --> 00:17:45,980
I'll get going then.

270
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:48,274
You have a meeting
with the contractors later,

271
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:49,151
so don't forget.

272
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:53,322
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

273
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:55,532
- You're all so close.
- Yes.

274
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:11,048
- It's beautiful.
- It's shining.

275
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,217
- You did it, Boss.
- You did it.

276
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,761
It's not over yet, so stay sharp.

277
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,054
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

278
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:19,680
Let's start wrapping things up.

279
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:21,849
Once we get the money
from the bank tomorrow morning,

280
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,352
- we're leaving immediately.
- Yes, sir.

281
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:24,770
It's a large amount.

282
00:18:25,437 --> 00:18:27,939
- Gyeong-nam, prepare a bag for the cash.
- Yes, sir.

283
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:30,274
Big Guy, sell off everything in the home.

284
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:31,275
Yes, sir.

285
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:33,570
- Je-gil, get the facility manager's stamp.
- Yes, sir.

286
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:35,364
The manager…

287
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:39,785
just threw his stamp to the side
on his desk earlier.

288
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:43,163
- Leave it to me, sir.
- He's so careless.

289
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:46,208
What about the Lizard and Ms. Kang?

290
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,752
- You shouldn't enter.
- It's fine.

291
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:51,170
It's authorized personnel only.

292
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:55,300
I'm the one who made him the president.
What do we call that again?

293
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:56,759
Kingmaker?

294
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:59,387
Yes. I'm the kingmaker,
so of course, I'm authorized.

295
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,265
Don't you agree, Mr. Park?

296
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:03,976
It's fine. You can go.

297
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,815
Mr. Park.

298
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:13,277
This is a gift
for your new position. Here.

299
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:16,363
What is this?

300
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:18,615
Unwrap it. Go on.

301
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:23,411
Our club members all felt so grateful,

302
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:26,206
so we pitched in to get this made for you.

303
00:19:27,374 --> 00:19:29,584
PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

304
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:31,044
Wow, a phoenix…

305
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,839
Not even the President
would have a plaque like that.

306
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:38,217
The position makes the person.

307
00:19:38,218 --> 00:19:42,973
You need something cool
like this right here…

308
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:46,768
to give your desk some presence.

309
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:54,400
Congratulations.

310
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:58,238
Come on, Mr. Park. Congratulations.

311
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:04,076
It's nice, isn't it?

312
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:05,912
So…

313
00:20:05,913 --> 00:20:09,498
we have to find something to pick at.

314
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:14,796
We have to paint
Park Hae-kang's election as illegal.

315
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:19,842
Then what should we pick at,
and how should we play it?

316
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:24,472
Maybe we can make an issue
of his candidate registration form.

317
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:27,058
How about Park Hae-kang's photo size?

318
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:30,061
He used a larger photo than yours.

319
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,229
What do you think?

320
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:34,065
He did violate the rules, didn't he?

321
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:35,524
We can't solve this problem

322
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:38,111
by making an issue
of something so trivial.

323
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,280
Not something like that.

324
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:45,576
We need something
that can bring him down in one go.

325
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:46,702
Something critical.

326
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:50,749
Mr. Lee, you took a lot of kickbacks
from Hansong Equipment, didn't you?

327
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:52,833
And Ms. Kim.

328
00:20:52,834 --> 00:20:56,837
I know you accepted a lot of money
from Director Park

329
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:58,881
during the bidding
for the kindergarten contract.

330
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:01,259
And Mr. Oh,

331
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:04,220
you pulled some strings
to get your sibling hired

332
00:21:04,221 --> 00:21:05,888
at the landscaping company.

333
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:08,392
I can easily come up
with a long list of stuff like this

334
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:11,186
just by thinking for a second.

335
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:15,691
But you look much too relaxed right now.

336
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:18,694
I really…

337
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:22,406
Listen.

338
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:27,660
If we can't get rid of Park Hae-kang,

339
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:30,454
if we fail to drag him down
from that position,

340
00:21:30,455 --> 00:21:33,040
we're all dead!

341
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:34,793
We're all going down.

342
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:37,086
Do you understand?

343
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,631
Ever heard the saying,
"Power never lasts"?

344
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:42,676
It means no one can stay in power forever.

345
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:47,472
President Park, you really are smart.

346
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:51,726
They say power cannot last ten years.

347
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:55,814
But foolish humans always grow corrupt,

348
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:57,606
thinking it will last forever.

349
00:21:57,607 --> 00:22:01,610
That is why I'm offering to manage

350
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:03,946
that kind of stuff for you.

351
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:05,657
- What stuff?
- You know.

352
00:22:08,243 --> 00:22:10,287
Family risk.

353
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:14,415
Politicians back then
all had family scandals.

354
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:18,879
No matter how good a politician you are,
one family scandal can bring you down.

355
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:21,130
Well, I guess so.

356
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:23,424
But that has nothing to do with us.

357
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:25,551
Of course, it does.

358
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:30,264
Power and corruption
are practically inseparable.

359
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:35,144
That is why I'm offering to become
your Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs

360
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:38,856
and manage such issues for you.

361
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:40,567
- Senior Secretary?
- Senior Secretary?

362
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:45,488
Yes. Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs.
Isn't that nice?

363
00:22:45,489 --> 00:22:49,492
I just want to see you
for a long time, that's all.

364
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:50,993
So let me do that for you.

365
00:22:50,994 --> 00:22:53,747
Okay? I'll be the Senior Secretary
for Civil Affairs.

366
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:57,875
Are you ready, sir?

367
00:22:57,876 --> 00:23:01,588
- You're here too, Ms. Jang.
- Yes, Mr. Choi.

368
00:23:03,256 --> 00:23:04,091
President Park,

369
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:05,759
are you ready?

370
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:11,181
Let's go!

371
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:16,644
Will it be okay to leave her be?

372
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:18,521
- This is bad.
- What's "Senior Secretary"?

373
00:23:18,522 --> 00:23:20,523
It's fine. We're leaving tomorrow.

374
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:23,943
- You guys go and get ready.
- Where's my coat? Bring my coat!

375
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:25,654
- Give me that.
- Boss.

376
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:29,032
- I can…
- Coming!

377
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:35,996
As you know, there are three floors

378
00:23:35,997 --> 00:23:39,708
with 121 shops in our apartment complex.

379
00:23:39,709 --> 00:23:41,044
This way, sir.

380
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:44,589
Gosh.

381
00:23:48,385 --> 00:23:51,387
Congratulations on becoming
the residents' association president!

382
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:53,265
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

383
00:23:56,518 --> 00:23:59,311
I'm True Value State's new president,
Park Hae-kang.

384
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:00,521
Nice to meet you all.

385
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:01,565
Applause!

386
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,776
We look forward to working with you.

387
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:09,072
This is our merchants' association
membership list.

388
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:13,617
If you visit any of our shops
and tell us you're the president,

389
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:15,162
everything will be on the house.

390
00:24:16,329 --> 00:24:17,622
On the house? Why?

391
00:24:18,623 --> 00:24:20,542
Because you're the president.

392
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:23,461
That includes your family too.

393
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:31,178
Our president doesn't accept
bribes of any kind.

394
00:24:33,930 --> 00:24:35,348
- Let's go.
- Right.

395
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:40,270
Our president is here.

396
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:47,693
Everyone,
as his Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs,

397
00:24:47,694 --> 00:24:49,821
let me make an important announcement.

398
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:53,574
President Park will not accept
bribes of any kind.

399
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:56,786
Take back everything you brought.

400
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:00,414
Take them back.

401
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:02,959
We look forward to working with you,
President Park!

402
00:25:06,755 --> 00:25:09,007
Let's go, True Value!

403
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:19,184
Sir.

404
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:20,809
Here.

405
00:25:20,810 --> 00:25:21,978
For your hard work.

406
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:28,318
What is this?

407
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,819
Take that

408
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:35,033
and announce that all the relics
found here were fabricated.

409
00:25:36,076 --> 00:25:39,037
Relics like this
can't have been discovered here.

410
00:25:40,830 --> 00:25:41,915
You really…

411
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:44,541
are quick-witted.

412
00:25:44,542 --> 00:25:46,794
You understood right away.

413
00:25:46,795 --> 00:25:49,964
Make an announcement
with what you just said.

414
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:55,303
No, I'm serious. It's almost impossible
for such relics to be found here.

415
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:58,014
What?

416
00:26:01,851 --> 00:26:04,770
The soil on the relics doesn't match,

417
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:07,356
and they're all from different periods.

418
00:26:07,357 --> 00:26:10,860
They can't have been found like this
unless someone planted them here.

419
00:26:12,153 --> 00:26:14,823
So someone planted them on purpose?

420
00:26:18,785 --> 00:26:20,870
If I catch whoever did this,

421
00:26:21,746 --> 00:26:23,206
I'm going to kill them.

422
00:26:34,092 --> 00:26:36,177
- Hello?
<i>- Hey, cop.</i>

423
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:38,680
You got the call from Mr. Song, right?

424
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:42,058
I need some help from you.

425
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:03,747
I LOVE YOU, RU-I

426
00:27:30,106 --> 00:27:31,149
Gyeong-buk.

427
00:27:36,112 --> 00:27:38,782
Ha-ri, what are you doing here?

428
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:41,241
I just made a parking account

429
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:43,952
with the benefits of a checking account
and a savings account.

430
00:27:43,953 --> 00:27:47,331
Right. You can make deposits
and withdrawals with daily interest.

431
00:27:47,332 --> 00:27:49,292
- I heard about it.
- Yeah, that one.

432
00:27:50,251 --> 00:27:53,962
A savings plan felt like too much,
so this was perfect for me.

433
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:56,090
I should make one too.
I really wanted this plushie.

434
00:27:56,091 --> 00:27:58,385
Hey. Just take it.

435
00:28:00,011 --> 00:28:01,345
You can make one online too.

436
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:02,722
- Really?
- Look.

437
00:28:09,145 --> 00:28:10,145
Hello?

438
00:28:10,146 --> 00:28:13,858
<i>This is True Value Kindergarten.
Is this Gyeong-buk's mom?</i>

439
00:28:14,401 --> 00:28:16,402
You've got the wrong number.

440
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:17,986
Wait! Hello?

441
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:20,031
Yes, I'm Gyeong-buk's mom.

442
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:23,243
You're his kindergarten teacher.

443
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:25,160
PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

444
00:28:25,161 --> 00:28:29,748
You must be exhausted from all that work,
President Park.

445
00:28:29,749 --> 00:28:31,918
Here, drink this.

446
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:35,088
Here. Cheers.

447
00:28:38,508 --> 00:28:40,135
Mr. Park, there's an emergency…

448
00:28:41,428 --> 00:28:42,678
Gosh.

449
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:48,517
Ma'am, you should be careful
of how you address him in public.

450
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:51,146
Did you just call him "Mr. Park"?

451
00:28:51,646 --> 00:28:52,647
You're married, you know.

452
00:28:56,317 --> 00:28:58,862
- Honey.
- Yes, dear?

453
00:28:59,612 --> 00:29:01,572
Gyeong-buk's having a sports day today.

454
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:04,701
All the other parents are playing games,
but we're the only ones absent.

455
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:07,829
Do you have something to say?

456
00:29:10,498 --> 00:29:13,585
That's what he was trying to say
this morning. Let's go.

457
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:16,503
Goodness. What are you doing?

458
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:19,381
President Park,
you have a huge pile of work to do.

459
00:29:19,382 --> 00:29:21,300
You can't go.

460
00:29:21,301 --> 00:29:24,679
Ma'am, mothers should
take care of such matters.

461
00:29:25,555 --> 00:29:28,098
Why should I go alone?
He has a father too.

462
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:33,521
For a man to achieve great things,
his family needs to make some sacrifices.

463
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:35,064
Ms. Jang.

464
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:38,942
Would events held by the kindergarten
mostly be attended

465
00:29:38,943 --> 00:29:40,944
- by parents of True Value?
- Of course.

466
00:29:40,945 --> 00:29:43,030
Then I'd say this is the perfect chance

467
00:29:43,031 --> 00:29:46,033
to solidify my position as the president

468
00:29:46,034 --> 00:29:47,868
and build the image of a loving father.

469
00:29:47,869 --> 00:29:49,621
What do you think, Ms. Jang?

470
00:29:53,082 --> 00:29:56,419
Then I'll clear out your entire afternoon.

471
00:30:08,431 --> 00:30:10,140
Wait for me!

472
00:30:10,141 --> 00:30:12,726
Riding the waves with Mom and Dad!

473
00:30:12,727 --> 00:30:13,686
Ready, go!

474
00:30:14,395 --> 00:30:17,022
Go, Team Pink! Go, Team Blue!

475
00:30:17,023 --> 00:30:19,066
Go, Team Pink!

476
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:21,151
Go! Look at Team Pink!

477
00:30:21,152 --> 00:30:22,528
Team Pink wins!

478
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:25,198
Team Pink won! Your team won, Gyeong-buk!

479
00:30:26,866 --> 00:30:29,409
- Let's do it together next.
- No.

480
00:30:29,410 --> 00:30:31,538
Why? Come on. Let's do it together.

481
00:30:43,007 --> 00:30:48,471
Everyone, True Value's
President Park Hae-kang is here.

482
00:30:48,972 --> 00:30:50,598
He's Gyeong-buk's father.

483
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,475
I'm Park Hae-kang.

484
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:54,727
Gyeong-buk!

485
00:30:57,730 --> 00:31:00,608
- They do kind of look alike.
- So he's his son.

486
00:31:02,569 --> 00:31:03,735
How did you know?

487
00:31:03,736 --> 00:31:05,113
I know everything.

488
00:31:10,410 --> 00:31:13,328
Gyeong-buk, why didn't you tell us
today was Sports Day?

489
00:31:13,329 --> 00:31:14,956
This isn't some huge secret.

490
00:31:15,832 --> 00:31:18,793
Because we're not a real family.

491
00:31:21,921 --> 00:31:25,133
I'll show you that I can do even better
since I'm not real.

492
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:27,593
They're all dead.

493
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:30,470
I'm going to defeat
all the mothers here today!

494
00:31:30,471 --> 00:31:31,472
Let's win!

495
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:37,520
EXPANDABLE LUGGAGE BAGS

496
00:31:38,187 --> 00:31:40,857
- Sir.
- What are you looking for?

497
00:31:41,441 --> 00:31:44,569
Are these all the bags you have?
They're smaller than I thought.

498
00:31:45,153 --> 00:31:46,404
Small?

499
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:49,532
You have no idea.

500
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:53,118
They can expand like magic.

501
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:54,662
You can fit ten billion in cash.

502
00:31:56,915 --> 00:31:59,333
Then I'll need at least two.

503
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:01,377
What? You have 20 billion?

504
00:32:02,629 --> 00:32:05,256
I wish. How much is it?

505
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:09,052
- Let's go eat, everyone.
- Yes, sir.

506
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:23,608
Geez. Why isn't this working?
This is driving me crazy.

507
00:32:24,859 --> 00:32:27,527
- Hello.
- You're the president's brother.

508
00:32:27,528 --> 00:32:29,821
He's not here right now, though.
Can I help you?

509
00:32:29,822 --> 00:32:32,575
Oh, he's not here.
I thought we could have lunch…

510
00:32:33,409 --> 00:32:34,535
Is that broken?

511
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:38,622
Thank you!

512
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:41,750
I would've gotten scolded again
if it weren't for you.

513
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,168
Is this for a meeting?

514
00:32:43,169 --> 00:32:44,879
It's our business plan for this year.

515
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:48,967
The president changed,
so we need a new one.

516
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:52,636
I didn't mean I'm unhappy
that the president changed.

517
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,179
Should I put this on his desk?

518
00:32:54,180 --> 00:32:56,599
You're really kind, unlike how you look.

519
00:33:07,318 --> 00:33:10,571
Is there anything else I can help with?
You can ask me anything.

520
00:33:13,741 --> 00:33:14,575
Excuse me.

521
00:33:15,702 --> 00:33:18,287
Are you Mr. Used Goods Fairy?

522
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:22,291
- You're Mr. No Discount?
- Yes.

523
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:24,292
The rice cooker…

524
00:33:24,293 --> 00:33:25,628
- The rice cooker.
- Yes.

525
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:29,381
- Here.
- Right.

526
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:30,590
- It works well.
- Okay.

527
00:33:30,591 --> 00:33:32,176
- No refunds or exchanges.
- Okay.

528
00:33:34,095 --> 00:33:34,929
Here.

529
00:33:35,638 --> 00:33:36,931
Thank you for the discount,

530
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:38,850
Mr. Used Goods Fairy.

531
00:33:41,102 --> 00:33:42,186
Please write a good review.

532
00:33:52,363 --> 00:33:55,074
A round of applause
for Gyeong-buk's father's kick!

533
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,169
Go!

534
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:53,508
Go, Mom! Go!

535
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:01,641
It's neck and neck!

536
00:35:04,310 --> 00:35:06,645
Gyeong-buk's mother is in first place!

537
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:08,898
Gyeong-buk's mother wins!

538
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:16,364
With more energy!

539
00:35:30,211 --> 00:35:32,338
Don't hesitate! Dance with more energy!

540
00:35:33,172 --> 00:35:34,381
Today's highlight.

541
00:35:34,382 --> 00:35:38,760
This game will be a four-legged race
to demonstrate family unity.

542
00:35:38,761 --> 00:35:43,140
Children from the winning teams
will get to choose their own reward.

543
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:46,643
You'll start at the sound of the whistle.

544
00:35:46,644 --> 00:35:47,770
Ready…

545
00:35:57,196 --> 00:36:00,782
Go!

546
00:36:00,783 --> 00:36:02,617
- Go!
- Go!

547
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:03,744
Park Hae-kang!

548
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:21,846
Oh my gosh.

549
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:31,522
Ms. Kang, get up.

550
00:36:32,523 --> 00:36:34,233
Help me.

551
00:36:35,318 --> 00:36:36,401
Sorry, Gyeong-buk.

552
00:36:36,402 --> 00:36:37,819
Are you okay?

553
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:39,238
Go!

554
00:36:40,239 --> 00:36:42,073
President Park!

555
00:36:42,074 --> 00:36:44,202
Beef! Ginseng!

556
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:47,621
We can't give up. Let's go!

557
00:36:47,622 --> 00:36:48,623
Let's go.

558
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:59,508
- There you go!
- We can do it!

559
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:16,274
The team in first place
chose the ginseng set.

560
00:37:16,275 --> 00:37:18,361
What will you choose, Gyeong-buk?

561
00:37:20,029 --> 00:37:20,863
Beef.

562
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:23,699
Choose the beef.

563
00:37:24,742 --> 00:37:25,576
The beef.

564
00:37:28,329 --> 00:37:30,038
The hair roller set.

565
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:31,831
I want this one.

566
00:37:31,832 --> 00:37:32,708
Gyeong-buk.

567
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:34,751
Why would you…

568
00:37:34,752 --> 00:37:37,212
There are lots of other great gifts.
Why that one?

569
00:37:37,213 --> 00:37:41,800
I saw on TV that other moms all have this,

570
00:37:41,801 --> 00:37:43,886
but my mom, Kang Ha-ri,
doesn't seem to have one.

571
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:48,515
- What a good son.
- So admirable.

572
00:37:48,516 --> 00:37:49,975
Sons are the best.

573
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:52,645
Goodness. What a good son.

574
00:37:55,731 --> 00:37:57,565
You're such a great son.

575
00:37:57,566 --> 00:38:00,151
You were worried about my hair. Let's see.

576
00:38:00,152 --> 00:38:02,279
There are different kinds of hair rollers.

577
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,448
This is much better than beef.

578
00:38:05,032 --> 00:38:06,116
Thank you, Gyeong-buk.

579
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:10,537
Our Gyeong-buk
is so considerate, isn't he?

580
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:13,708
Give our kind Gyeong-buk
a round of applause!

581
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:15,918
Yes, let's give a round of applause.

582
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:18,254
I'm so happy.

583
00:38:23,009 --> 00:38:25,260
He chose hair rollers
over beef and ginseng.

584
00:38:25,261 --> 00:38:28,139
Does Gyeong-buk like me that much?

585
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:30,725
How do I look? Pretty?

586
00:38:39,108 --> 00:38:40,526
What kind of reaction is that?

587
00:38:42,611 --> 00:38:45,780
I'll give my bangs some volume
before coming to work tomorrow.

588
00:38:45,781 --> 00:38:47,658
<i>Boss, everything's done.</i>

589
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:50,286
Ms. Kang.

590
00:38:51,954 --> 00:38:52,955
Yes?

591
00:38:59,086 --> 00:39:00,171
Ms. Kang.

592
00:39:01,047 --> 00:39:03,382
You don't have to come to work anymore.

593
00:39:04,633 --> 00:39:07,844
What? What do you mean?

594
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:09,596
It hasn't been two weeks yet.

595
00:39:09,597 --> 00:39:11,264
You don't have to fill the two weeks.

596
00:39:11,265 --> 00:39:14,225
I'll transfer the money to you by today.

597
00:39:14,226 --> 00:39:16,645
Great work. You can go now.

598
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:20,691
You're just sending me off right now?

599
00:39:21,484 --> 00:39:24,862
- My bag is still there--
- I'll have your things delivered to you.

600
00:39:30,117 --> 00:39:31,243
Take a cab home.

601
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:36,832
Goodbye then.

602
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:45,383
What?

603
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:06,570
Isn't that ridiculous?

604
00:40:07,488 --> 00:40:08,655
How could he do this?

605
00:40:08,656 --> 00:40:13,243
How can he just treat me like this

606
00:40:13,244 --> 00:40:15,787
after all the time we spent together?

607
00:40:15,788 --> 00:40:18,373
Was that all just a lie?

608
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:19,457
Yeah.

609
00:40:19,458 --> 00:40:21,752
Of course it was.
It was a stand-in service.

610
00:40:22,795 --> 00:40:24,295
Still…

611
00:40:24,296 --> 00:40:27,382
How could he just send me away
so coldly like that?

612
00:40:27,383 --> 00:40:28,550
Forget it.

613
00:40:28,551 --> 00:40:30,260
You got the rest of the payment.

614
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:32,179
You should focus on your studies now.

615
00:40:33,222 --> 00:40:35,141
I will, but…

616
00:40:35,850 --> 00:40:37,685
I just feel so upset.

617
00:41:10,384 --> 00:41:12,052
- Boss.
- Yes?

618
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,846
- Here.
- Right.

619
00:41:14,847 --> 00:41:16,182
Good job.

620
00:41:16,682 --> 00:41:18,433
You all did great.

621
00:41:18,434 --> 00:41:21,562
We just have to drop by the bank
tomorrow morning and leave.

622
00:41:22,771 --> 00:41:23,938
What about Gyeong-nam?

623
00:41:23,939 --> 00:41:25,399
He went to take Gyeong-buk back.

624
00:41:26,775 --> 00:41:28,402
But sir, what about Ms. Kang?

625
00:41:30,321 --> 00:41:31,697
- It's done.
- What?

626
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:34,241
You don't need to worry about it.

627
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:37,203
We didn't even get to say goodbye to her.

628
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:53,051
It's really stretchy.

629
00:41:53,052 --> 00:41:54,385
Looks yummy.

630
00:41:54,386 --> 00:41:55,763
- Eat up.
- Okay.

631
00:41:58,474 --> 00:41:59,557
It's good.

632
00:41:59,558 --> 00:42:01,435
- Is it? Eat as much as you want.
- Yes.

633
00:42:06,148 --> 00:42:07,024
Gyeong-buk.

634
00:42:09,151 --> 00:42:12,154
It was tough living in Seoul, wasn't it?

635
00:42:12,738 --> 00:42:13,905
What do you mean?

636
00:42:13,906 --> 00:42:18,159
I mean, there were lots of people at home.
Even a weird grandpa.

637
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:21,204
You suddenly had a mom and several uncles.

638
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:22,914
And I made you lie

639
00:42:22,915 --> 00:42:26,210
and call Uncle Hae-kang your dad.

640
00:42:27,002 --> 00:42:28,169
No.

641
00:42:28,170 --> 00:42:30,965
I was happy to have Mom, my uncles,

642
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:33,384
and Grandpa there.

643
00:42:34,593 --> 00:42:36,053
I want to do it again.

644
00:42:36,637 --> 00:42:38,639
I think I like having a family, Dad.

645
00:42:44,144 --> 00:42:46,980
We'll be a family again next time.

646
00:42:46,981 --> 00:42:48,983
Okay. Promise?

647
00:42:59,702 --> 00:43:01,579
I saw it. There's no need to hide it.

648
00:43:02,538 --> 00:43:05,124
You really should quit gambling now, sir.

649
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:08,586
Mr. Park.

650
00:43:09,837 --> 00:43:11,130
Did you just…

651
00:43:12,006 --> 00:43:13,507
speak politely to me?

652
00:43:14,842 --> 00:43:17,720
You're not young anymore.
Are you going to keep living like this?

653
00:43:18,679 --> 00:43:21,265
You're scaring me, Mr. Park.

654
00:43:23,934 --> 00:43:25,936
Did I do something wrong again?

655
00:43:26,645 --> 00:43:29,440
Don't kill me. You said you'd let me live.

656
00:43:30,190 --> 00:43:32,318
It's not that. Just sit comfortably.

657
00:43:32,901 --> 00:43:33,902
Come on.

658
00:43:39,241 --> 00:43:40,492
You did a great job.

659
00:43:41,243 --> 00:43:44,496
I'll cancel the debt you owe
to our gambling den.

660
00:43:45,539 --> 00:43:46,540
Mr. Park.

661
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:49,668
So you got everything.

662
00:43:52,796 --> 00:43:54,089
Is tomorrow the big day?

663
00:43:54,965 --> 00:43:58,009
Once we drop by the bank tomorrow
and get the money,

664
00:43:58,010 --> 00:43:59,553
I'll give you a portion.

665
00:44:01,513 --> 00:44:03,515
No, Mr. Park.

666
00:44:04,058 --> 00:44:07,102
It's fine. I'm really fine.

667
00:44:08,228 --> 00:44:11,773
I'm already grateful
that you let me stay and hide here.

668
00:44:11,774 --> 00:44:12,815
Are you sure?

669
00:44:12,816 --> 00:44:15,611
Yes. I'm really okay.

670
00:44:16,278 --> 00:44:17,655
Live a decent life now.

671
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:20,741
I will.

672
00:44:24,036 --> 00:44:26,288
You know I have contacts
everywhere, right?

673
00:44:27,373 --> 00:44:31,460
If I ever hear that you're gambling again,
then I'll really cut off your hands.

674
00:44:34,129 --> 00:44:35,130
Get some sleep.

675
00:44:54,441 --> 00:44:55,651
He's…

676
00:44:57,027 --> 00:44:58,862
really thoughtful.

677
00:45:04,159 --> 00:45:06,203
How handsome.

678
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:14,210
We'll hit the bank in the morning,
get the money, send it to Mr. Son,

679
00:45:14,211 --> 00:45:15,461
then leave Seoul.

680
00:45:15,462 --> 00:45:17,964
I found an island
where we can lie low for a while.

681
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:20,175
- And the Lizard?
- I told him to go to our car.

682
00:45:22,386 --> 00:45:25,179
Let's start over
after we get Yong-man back.

683
00:45:25,180 --> 00:45:26,432
- Yes, Boss.
- Yes, Boss.

684
00:45:27,558 --> 00:45:28,642
Let's go.

685
00:46:03,760 --> 00:46:05,636
How may I help you?

686
00:46:05,637 --> 00:46:07,764
I'd like to withdraw
the entire amount in cash.

687
00:46:11,185 --> 00:46:13,479
- The entire amount?
- Yes.

688
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:17,691
Do you live in an apartment?

689
00:46:18,859 --> 00:46:20,527
- Yes.
- Then you'd know.

690
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:25,115
We have some major construction coming up.
I'm the residents' association president.

691
00:46:25,699 --> 00:46:28,535
As you know,
it costs a fortune to replace an elevator.

692
00:46:31,163 --> 00:46:33,331
- Should I give you this bag?
- No, it's fine.

693
00:46:33,332 --> 00:46:34,875
- Just a moment.
- All right.

694
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:53,809
What is this?

695
00:46:53,810 --> 00:46:56,187
You wanted the entire amount.

696
00:46:56,188 --> 00:46:59,191
It's 2,530 won.

697
00:47:15,374 --> 00:47:16,666
I want to withdraw everything.

698
00:47:16,667 --> 00:47:19,503
Your balance is 7,280 won.

699
00:47:20,879 --> 00:47:22,713
<i>He's taking a long time.</i>

700
00:47:22,714 --> 00:47:24,298
Is it too heavy to carry on his own?

701
00:47:24,299 --> 00:47:26,009
Here's your 7,650 won.

702
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:31,931
Here's your full balance. 4,910 won.

703
00:47:31,932 --> 00:47:33,182
<i>Of course, it's heavy.</i>

704
00:47:33,183 --> 00:47:34,434
Should we have gone with him?

705
00:47:39,565 --> 00:47:42,818
The money is in different banks,
so obviously, it'll take a while.

706
00:47:44,403 --> 00:47:46,280
Here's your total of 9,220 won.

707
00:47:49,741 --> 00:47:50,742
MIRAE BANK

708
00:47:58,333 --> 00:47:59,584
This can't be true.

709
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:01,961
<i>The long-term repair reserve fund?</i>

710
00:48:01,962 --> 00:48:04,255
<i>There's 17,857,420,000 won.</i>

711
00:48:04,256 --> 00:48:06,716
They said it was there. Where is it?

712
00:48:06,717 --> 00:48:08,926
I went through so much for that money.

713
00:48:08,927 --> 00:48:13,055
I'm Candidate 3 for District 4,
Park Hae-kang!

714
00:48:13,056 --> 00:48:14,390
<i>I'll take care of this problem!</i>

715
00:48:14,391 --> 00:48:15,225
So dig.

716
00:48:16,435 --> 00:48:17,810
- Park Hae-kang!
- Park Hae-kang!

717
00:48:17,811 --> 00:48:20,230
Move Exit 3 to True Value!

718
00:48:21,607 --> 00:48:22,899
I worked so hard for this.

719
00:48:26,111 --> 00:48:28,614
The 17,857,420,000 won…

720
00:48:29,364 --> 00:48:30,699
Where is my money?

721
00:48:33,368 --> 00:48:36,412
My 17,857,420,000 won!

722
00:48:36,413 --> 00:48:38,081
Where is it?

723
00:48:42,044 --> 00:48:44,754
Mr. Park! Please let me out!

724
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:46,797
I'm going to suffocate to death!

725
00:48:46,798 --> 00:48:48,466
Please!

726
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:49,509
Please…

727
00:48:54,806 --> 00:48:56,433
I'm claustrophobic.

728
00:48:58,769 --> 00:49:00,645
Why are we on the roof again?

729
00:49:00,646 --> 00:49:03,523
I'm scared of heights too!

730
00:49:05,609 --> 00:49:07,152
The money isn't there!

731
00:49:07,736 --> 00:49:12,615
The 17,857,420,000 won.
It's not there. Why?

732
00:49:12,616 --> 00:49:15,117
I'm frustrated too.

733
00:49:15,118 --> 00:49:19,038
We all heard it over the phone that day.
She said they had 17.8 billion.

734
00:49:19,039 --> 00:49:21,624
You should be looking
for the one who took it

735
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:24,168
instead of taking it out on me.

736
00:49:24,169 --> 00:49:26,671
Fine. Then how do we find this person?

737
00:49:26,672 --> 00:49:28,423
Who do you think took it?

738
00:49:28,965 --> 00:49:30,634
It's a huge amount.

739
00:49:31,218 --> 00:49:35,054
Unless the president, facility manager,
and the accountant worked together…

740
00:49:35,055 --> 00:49:37,224
So they took it together?

741
00:49:38,141 --> 00:49:41,687
I just mean it's not certain,
but it's a possibility.

742
00:49:42,562 --> 00:49:44,188
- Zip it up.
- You little…

743
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:46,148
Wait!

744
00:49:46,149 --> 00:49:49,861
I'm a professional in this field!
How would you get it without me?

745
00:49:53,657 --> 00:49:55,784
What do we do now, Boss?

746
00:49:56,368 --> 00:49:57,618
We need to find it.

747
00:49:57,619 --> 00:49:59,286
I need my money!

748
00:49:59,287 --> 00:50:02,415
But if they really did take it,
how would we find it?

749
00:50:02,416 --> 00:50:04,376
Well, first…

750
00:50:05,419 --> 00:50:07,838
Let's look into those three.

751
00:50:08,547 --> 00:50:09,589
All right then.

752
00:50:10,632 --> 00:50:12,425
It's going to take a while.

753
00:50:12,426 --> 00:50:15,261
Boss, you have to maintain
your position as the president

754
00:50:15,262 --> 00:50:16,596
to make the investigation easier.

755
00:50:17,514 --> 00:50:20,934
Then we'll have to continue
the intermittent family act.

756
00:50:23,520 --> 00:50:24,478
I CAN DO IT!

757
00:50:24,479 --> 00:50:25,939
<i>Read the textbook and follow along.</i>

758
00:50:26,565 --> 00:50:28,274
<i>Unfair dismissal is clearly defined</i>

759
00:50:28,275 --> 00:50:31,694
<i>in Article 23, Paragraph 1
of the Labor Standards Act.</i>

760
00:50:31,695 --> 00:50:35,949
<i>Simply put,
it's a dismissal without a valid reason.</i>

761
00:50:38,201 --> 00:50:40,454
Right. This is an unfair dismissal.

762
00:50:41,204 --> 00:50:43,457
That's why I felt so angry.

763
00:50:44,207 --> 00:50:46,585
Why didn't I think
of the Labor Standards Act?

764
00:50:47,169 --> 00:50:49,129
I should've protested by citing it.

765
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:52,673
This is all because I didn't study enough.

766
00:50:52,674 --> 00:50:54,801
I should focus on studying.

767
00:50:59,264 --> 00:51:01,141
Why am I using this right now?

768
00:51:02,184 --> 00:51:04,101
Well, kids are innocent.

769
00:51:04,102 --> 00:51:05,437
Gyeong-buk is innocent.

770
00:51:10,150 --> 00:51:12,902
<i>I brought your things.
Let's talk for a moment.</i>

771
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:15,280
What? He's in front of my house right now?

772
00:51:23,622 --> 00:51:25,582
CIVIL LAW KEY POINTS

773
00:51:29,419 --> 00:51:30,628
What's going on?

774
00:51:30,629 --> 00:51:33,131
Did you change your job
to an express delivery guy?

775
00:51:41,056 --> 00:51:42,599
How have you been?

776
00:51:43,183 --> 00:51:44,809
What kind of greeting is that?

777
00:51:44,810 --> 00:51:45,936
We saw each other yesterday.

778
00:51:49,481 --> 00:51:51,399
We didn't see each other this morning.

779
00:51:58,198 --> 00:52:00,992
I came in person
because I had something to tell you.

780
00:52:02,702 --> 00:52:05,246
Good. I have something to say too.

781
00:52:05,247 --> 00:52:07,456
Article 23, Paragraph 1
of the Labor Standards Act

782
00:52:07,457 --> 00:52:08,999
states that an employer

783
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,878
shall not dismiss an employee
without justifiable cause.

784
00:52:12,879 --> 00:52:14,297
What's the reason for my dismissal?

785
00:52:16,007 --> 00:52:17,424
I made a mistake.

786
00:52:17,425 --> 00:52:20,720
We still need you, Ms. Kang.

787
00:52:21,388 --> 00:52:23,222
Please come back to work.

788
00:52:23,223 --> 00:52:24,057
What?

789
00:52:25,141 --> 00:52:27,935
You fired me yesterday,
and now you want me to come back?

790
00:52:27,936 --> 00:52:29,103
I'm sorry.

791
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:30,729
You must be quite upset.

792
00:52:30,730 --> 00:52:32,815
I promise to compensate you for--

793
00:52:32,816 --> 00:52:34,692
Excuse me, Mr. Park.

794
00:52:34,693 --> 00:52:36,068
I do like money,

795
00:52:36,069 --> 00:52:38,654
but don't try to solve everything
with your money.

796
00:52:38,655 --> 00:52:40,322
You should be apologizing

797
00:52:40,323 --> 00:52:42,617
and reflecting
for firing someone like that.

798
00:52:45,745 --> 00:52:47,747
I apologize, Ms. Kang.

799
00:52:49,291 --> 00:52:50,667
I am sincerely sorry

800
00:52:51,710 --> 00:52:54,504
if I upset you.

801
00:52:56,131 --> 00:52:57,591
Please work for two more weeks.

802
00:53:00,093 --> 00:53:03,638
It would be harsh to ignore you
when you're begging me like this.

803
00:53:04,472 --> 00:53:06,850
I'll work for two more weeks
as I promised.

804
00:53:09,102 --> 00:53:10,103
Thank you.

805
00:53:15,066 --> 00:53:16,443
Whose car is that?

806
00:53:17,027 --> 00:53:18,486
I think it's an employee's.

807
00:53:20,530 --> 00:53:23,282
Hello, everyone.

808
00:53:23,283 --> 00:53:24,951
Please, sit.

809
00:53:29,164 --> 00:53:32,166
You got all the security footage,
didn't you?

810
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,168
Yes.

811
00:53:34,252 --> 00:53:35,837
Did you find anything interesting?

812
00:53:36,796 --> 00:53:40,091
Among the cars
entering and leaving Oman New Town,

813
00:53:41,176 --> 00:53:44,470
there's one car going in and out
besides the construction vehicles.

814
00:53:44,471 --> 00:53:45,847
We're looking into it now.

815
00:53:46,640 --> 00:53:47,974
Really?

816
00:53:51,353 --> 00:53:55,357
Then we'll find out who that jerk is soon.

817
00:53:58,652 --> 00:53:59,653
President Park.

818
00:54:04,115 --> 00:54:05,157
Hello, Mr. Choi.

819
00:54:05,158 --> 00:54:08,035
What brings you here so early?

820
00:54:08,036 --> 00:54:10,956
And you're here alone
without your family today.

821
00:54:12,123 --> 00:54:16,460
I couldn't sleep all night
thinking about how to run this place,

822
00:54:16,461 --> 00:54:18,046
so I just came to work early.

823
00:54:20,256 --> 00:54:23,343
You were thinking about that all night?

824
00:54:25,887 --> 00:54:26,888
Mr. Choi.

825
00:54:27,931 --> 00:54:32,560
What's the most urgent issue
in our apartment complex right now?

826
00:54:33,728 --> 00:54:36,815
Well, there's the elevator repair issue.

827
00:54:38,608 --> 00:54:40,652
- Elevator repair?
- Yes.

828
00:54:42,487 --> 00:54:44,321
How do we pay for that?

829
00:54:44,322 --> 00:54:45,740
With the reserve fund.

830
00:54:46,449 --> 00:54:48,660
- The long-term repair reserve fund?
- Yes.

831
00:54:50,078 --> 00:54:51,578
It would cost quite a lot.

832
00:54:51,579 --> 00:54:54,040
Will there be any issues using the fund?

833
00:54:55,125 --> 00:54:56,625
Not at all.

834
00:54:56,626 --> 00:54:59,545
This is exactly
what the reserve fund is for.

835
00:54:59,546 --> 00:55:03,841
But the elevator's been
breaking down quite often,

836
00:55:03,842 --> 00:55:07,178
so the repair company
agreed to fix it for free this time.

837
00:55:08,972 --> 00:55:11,181
So when we need to use the reserve fund,

838
00:55:11,182 --> 00:55:14,560
I stamp it as the president,
then you stamp it,

839
00:55:14,561 --> 00:55:17,855
and the accounting manager
processes the payment?

840
00:55:17,856 --> 00:55:20,733
Yes, that's right.
When Ha-jeong returns, I mean.

841
00:55:20,734 --> 00:55:23,611
- Ha-jeong? The accounting manager?
- Yes.

842
00:55:24,446 --> 00:55:26,655
Come to think of it, I've never met her.

843
00:55:26,656 --> 00:55:31,368
Well, Ha-jeong went on vacation
for the first time in years.

844
00:55:31,369 --> 00:55:33,413
She'll be returning soon.

845
00:55:35,582 --> 00:55:37,000
Her desk is over there.

846
00:55:38,001 --> 00:55:39,418
- I see. "Kang Ha-jeong."
- Yes.

847
00:55:39,419 --> 00:55:41,671
She's right there below me
on the organizational chart.

848
00:55:44,090 --> 00:55:46,509
ACCOUNTING MANAGER
KANG HA-JEONG

849
00:55:47,802 --> 00:55:49,304
I'd love to meet her soon.

850
00:55:53,141 --> 00:55:58,312
He skipped work
after he was just elected president.

851
00:55:58,313 --> 00:56:01,274
Did he come to work on time today?

852
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:04,902
You cut open Gyeong-buk's piggy bank?

853
00:56:04,903 --> 00:56:07,071
Gyeong-nam, stop.

854
00:56:07,072 --> 00:56:09,365
Don't get blood on your hands.

855
00:56:10,075 --> 00:56:11,159
Just like this.

856
00:56:11,659 --> 00:56:13,952
I'll cut him open exactly the same way
and go to jail.

857
00:56:13,953 --> 00:56:15,120
- Move.
- Seriously?

858
00:56:15,121 --> 00:56:16,122
Stop it.

859
00:56:17,123 --> 00:56:19,833
To be honest, I needed some money.

860
00:56:19,834 --> 00:56:21,211
This place…

861
00:56:22,921 --> 00:56:25,964
is actually a gambling den.

862
00:56:25,965 --> 00:56:28,550
A few old folks
are playing gambling games,

863
00:56:28,551 --> 00:56:30,177
but they're terrible at them.

864
00:56:30,178 --> 00:56:32,055
I can easily earn money here.

865
00:56:33,181 --> 00:56:35,182
Shut that mouth.

866
00:56:35,183 --> 00:56:37,685
Hey, stop. Someone might see.

867
00:56:40,522 --> 00:56:43,274
Right, Father. So…

868
00:56:44,234 --> 00:56:46,361
Were you trying to gamble again?

869
00:56:47,237 --> 00:56:49,447
Do you want your hands cut off?

870
00:56:51,324 --> 00:56:52,534
Go home.

871
00:57:08,508 --> 00:57:09,509
My gosh.

872
00:57:10,135 --> 00:57:12,220
Those jerks.

873
00:57:13,388 --> 00:57:16,349
How could they threaten their dad,
even if he has a gambling problem?

874
00:57:18,351 --> 00:57:20,019
That is unforgivable, seriously.

875
00:57:21,146 --> 00:57:22,188
Mom!

876
00:57:23,731 --> 00:57:24,941
Here. Take this.

877
00:57:27,110 --> 00:57:28,570
I just found it.

878
00:57:29,320 --> 00:57:31,864
My dad told me
I shouldn't eat stuff lying around.

879
00:57:31,865 --> 00:57:34,409
Hey, don't you get what I mean?

880
00:57:35,326 --> 00:57:36,953
I like you.

881
00:57:37,954 --> 00:57:39,789
I only like my mom, Kang Ha-ri.

882
00:57:43,334 --> 00:57:44,418
Bye, Gyeong-buk.

883
00:57:44,419 --> 00:57:46,546
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

884
00:57:48,173 --> 00:57:49,340
- I don't know.
- Did you fight?

885
00:57:49,924 --> 00:57:51,759
- What?
- Why do you look so upset?

886
00:57:54,012 --> 00:57:56,181
- Did you eat a lot for lunch?
- Mom!

887
00:57:57,849 --> 00:57:59,976
Mom!

888
00:58:04,147 --> 00:58:07,150
So Hye-jun said she liked you,
but you rejected her?

889
00:58:08,693 --> 00:58:10,403
Why? Is she not pretty?

890
00:58:10,987 --> 00:58:13,072
I like you the most, Mom.

891
00:58:13,656 --> 00:58:15,200
You're the prettiest.

892
00:58:15,783 --> 00:58:17,451
Oh my gosh.

893
00:58:17,452 --> 00:58:20,370
You're so silly.

894
00:58:20,371 --> 00:58:21,914
But Gyeong-buk,

895
00:58:21,915 --> 00:58:24,583
I really can't get used to this.

896
00:58:24,584 --> 00:58:27,628
Can't you just call me Ha-ri
when no one's around?

897
00:58:27,629 --> 00:58:30,714
It's so awkward when you call me Mom.

898
00:58:30,715 --> 00:58:33,218
- Can you do that for me?
- Okay, Ha-ri.

899
00:58:33,968 --> 00:58:35,177
I'll buy you chocolate milk.

900
00:58:35,178 --> 00:58:37,096
- Yes!
- Yes!

901
00:58:44,062 --> 00:58:46,189
What the heck did I just hear?

902
00:58:46,981 --> 00:58:47,982
"Ha-ri"?

903
00:58:48,816 --> 00:58:50,151
He called her by her first name?

904
00:58:53,238 --> 00:58:55,072
It's so sweet, Mom.

905
00:58:55,073 --> 00:58:56,074
"Ha-ri."

906
00:58:56,950 --> 00:58:58,284
It's so sweet, Ha-ri.

907
00:59:01,162 --> 00:59:02,413
It's tasty, right?

908
00:59:05,625 --> 00:59:06,708
Ha-ri.

909
00:59:06,709 --> 00:59:09,212
Ha-jeong, what are you doing here?

910
00:59:09,796 --> 00:59:10,964
What about you?

911
00:59:11,923 --> 00:59:13,508
Who is that, Mom?

912
00:59:16,219 --> 00:59:17,387
"Mom"?

913
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:25,562
Well, it's…

914
00:59:36,864 --> 00:59:39,199
It's so strange.

915
00:59:39,200 --> 00:59:41,828
Do you want your hands cut off?

916
00:59:42,745 --> 00:59:46,124
The way those jerks spoke to their father…

917
00:59:46,708 --> 00:59:49,293
Can't you just call me Ha-ri
when no one's around?

918
00:59:49,294 --> 00:59:52,046
And she told him to call her
by her first name.

919
00:59:55,717 --> 00:59:58,427
Whatever. Forget it.

920
00:59:58,428 --> 00:59:59,762
It's not my business.

921
01:00:01,973 --> 01:00:02,807
Right.

922
01:00:03,808 --> 01:00:06,894
What family doesn't have problems?

923
01:00:09,188 --> 01:00:11,149
Right. Every family does.

924
01:00:17,071 --> 01:00:18,406
But still…

925
01:00:19,157 --> 01:00:21,867
It's the president's family.

926
01:00:21,868 --> 01:00:25,079
The president's family
shouldn't have issues like that.

927
01:00:28,875 --> 01:00:33,171
- Dad, the elevator's broken.
- It's broken?

928
01:00:33,755 --> 01:00:36,090
Mr. Park, let me talk to you for a second.

929
01:00:47,852 --> 01:00:49,144
What is it?

930
01:00:49,145 --> 01:00:51,648
We looked into the owner of that car, sir.

931
01:00:53,691 --> 01:00:55,942
What? It's Park Hae-kang.

932
01:00:55,943 --> 01:00:58,028
It's the only one
besides the construction vehicles

933
01:00:58,029 --> 01:01:01,032
and the cars whose owners
we've identified.

934
01:01:07,747 --> 01:01:08,997
Then does that mean

935
01:01:08,998 --> 01:01:12,751
Park Hae-kang planted them
to raise housing prices

936
01:01:12,752 --> 01:01:15,003
and get elected as the president?

937
01:01:15,004 --> 01:01:17,215
Yes, it seems so.

938
01:01:20,218 --> 01:01:21,511
Wow.

939
01:01:22,845 --> 01:01:24,514
President Park Hae-kang…

940
01:01:26,015 --> 01:01:28,184
He's quite something.

941
01:01:30,353 --> 01:01:33,271
Mr. Park, I'm sorry,
but I can't work here anymore.

942
01:01:33,272 --> 01:01:34,857
What do you mean?

943
01:01:36,067 --> 01:01:37,651
Something came up.

944
01:01:37,652 --> 01:01:39,528
You can't just quit like this.

945
01:01:39,529 --> 01:01:41,738
You fired me suddenly too.

946
01:01:41,739 --> 01:01:43,865
So just consider us even now.

947
01:01:43,866 --> 01:01:46,827
You already received your payment.
You should do your job.

948
01:01:46,828 --> 01:01:49,246
You said you're a professional.

949
01:01:49,247 --> 01:01:51,999
Even a professional
can have an emergency sometimes!

950
01:01:53,835 --> 01:01:55,962
What is that emergency? Let me hear it.

951
01:01:57,422 --> 01:01:58,422
I can't tell you.

952
01:01:58,423 --> 01:02:00,924
What's the point in being your wife
for two more weeks?

953
01:02:00,925 --> 01:02:04,387
You already got the position
that you wanted so badly.

954
01:02:05,888 --> 01:02:08,557
Our family still needs you, Ms. Kang.

955
01:02:08,558 --> 01:02:12,353
Mr. Park, that family you speak of
is fake anyway!

956
01:02:13,604 --> 01:02:14,938
What?

957
01:02:14,939 --> 01:02:16,231
"Fake"?

958
01:02:16,232 --> 01:02:18,109
Oh my goodness. You…

959
01:02:19,694 --> 01:02:21,863
So you guys

960
01:02:22,655 --> 01:02:24,157
were a fake family?

961
01:02:28,661 --> 01:02:31,372
THE APARTMENT JOB

962
01:02:55,480 --> 01:02:57,481
<i>Emptying out the entire account
makes no sense.</i>

963
01:02:57,482 --> 01:03:00,108
<i>Make something that requires you
to use the fund.</i>

964
01:03:00,109 --> 01:03:01,861
- Let's find…
- Defects!

965
01:03:02,528 --> 01:03:05,322
<i>Since it's an emergency,
I'll allow a wide range of touching.</i>

966
01:03:05,323 --> 01:03:07,032
I can tell that you're faking it.

967
01:03:07,033 --> 01:03:08,158
- Ms. Jang!
- Ms. Jang!

968
01:03:08,159 --> 01:03:11,287
<i>He would've found out
that the account is empty.</i>

969
01:03:12,914 --> 01:03:16,625
The reserve fund. He became the president
to pocket the fund.

970
01:03:16,626 --> 01:03:17,542
<i>We don't have time.</i>

971
01:03:17,543 --> 01:03:19,879
<i>Find anything that can be paid for
out of the reserve fund.</i>

972
01:03:21,088 --> 01:03:23,507
<i>Precisely 123 households
have a heating bill of zero.</i>

973
01:03:23,508 --> 01:03:24,841
President Park.

974
01:03:24,842 --> 01:03:27,594
Then will you become
another Heating Bill Martyr?

975
01:03:27,595 --> 01:03:29,346
Heating Bill Martyr…

976
01:03:29,347 --> 01:03:30,764
<i>I don't get how Park found out.</i>

977
01:03:30,765 --> 01:03:32,057
I won't let it happen again--

978
01:03:32,058 --> 01:03:33,183
I'm enjoying this,

979
01:03:33,184 --> 01:03:35,228
<i>so just let Park Hae-kang
do what he wants.</i>

980
01:03:38,731 --> 01:03:40,733
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
